{
  "title": "Quadriceps Tendon Rupture",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3023/quadriceps-tendon-rupture",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 4 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A quadriceps tendon rupture is a traumatic injury of the quadriceps insertion on the patella leading to a disruption in the knee extensor mechanism.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with a palpable defect 2 cm proximal to the superior pole of the patella with inability to perform a straight leg raise and presence of patella baja on knee radiographs.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be nonoperative in patients with partial tears and intact extensor mechanism. Operative repair is indicated if there is disruption of the extensor mechanism.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "quadriceps tendon rupture is **more common than patellar tendon rupture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually occurs in patients > 40 years of age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "males > females (up to 8:1)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "occurs in nondominant limb more than twice as often",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually at insertion of tendon to the patella",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**renal failure**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**diabetes**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**rheumatoid arthritis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hyperparathyroidism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "connective tissue disorders",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "steroid use",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "intraarticular injections (in 20-33%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**eccentric loading** of the knee extensor mechanism",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "often occurs when the foot is planted and knee is slightly bent",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "in younger patients the mechanism is usually direct trauma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Rupture classified as either",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "partial",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "complete",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Quadriceps tendon",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "has been described as having 2 to 4 distinct layers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "important when distinguishing between partial and complete tear and when repairing tendon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often report a history of pain leading up to rupture consistent with an underlying tendonopathy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tenderness at site of rupture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**palpable defect** usually within 2 cm of superior pole of patella",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "unable to extend the knee against resistance",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "unable to perform **straight leg raise with complete rupture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral of knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "will show patella baja",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "when there is uncertainty regarding diagnosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "helps differentiate between a partial and complete tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "knee immobilization in brace",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "partial tear with intact knee extensor mechanism",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "patients who cannot tolerate surgery",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "primary repair with reattachment to patella",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "complete rupture with loss of extensor mechanism",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Primary repair of acute rupture**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "midline incision to knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "transpatellar drill holes or suture anchors",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "nonabsorbable sutures in tendon in a running locking fashion with ends free to be passed through osseous drill holes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**repair with suture anchors has been shown to have decreased gap formation and increased ultimate loads to failure**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "suture anchor and transosseous techniques have equivalent functional and clinical outcomes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "recent evidence suggests there may be improved PROMs with suture anchor repair",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "retinaculum is repaired with heavy absorbable sutures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ideally the knee should flex to 90 degrees after repair",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "postoperative care",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "initial immobilization in brace, cast, or splint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "eventual progressive flexibility and strengthening exercises",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Primary repair of chronic rupture**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "midline to knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often the tendon retracts proximally",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ruptures >2 weeks old can retract 5cm",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "repaired with a similar technique to acute ruptures but a **tendon lengthening procedure** may be necessary",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Codivilla procedure (V-Y lengthening)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**auto or allograft tissue** may be needed to secure quadriceps tendon to patella",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Strength deficit**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "33%-50% of patients",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Stiffness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Functional impairment**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "50% of patients are unable to return to prior level of activity/ sports",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Re-rupture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Risk is increased in the setting of pre-existing inflammatory arthropathy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
